id: pm-jev-82ip
title: Evaluate decisions against public tracker ground truth
description: "Deterministic SDK-only public tracker evaluation for triage, typed links and known duplicates, with provenance, reliability and coverage metrics."
type: Feature
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags[3]: added,calibration,eval
created_at: "2026-10-18T03:02:20.523Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-18T05:45:56.900Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: "Public committed tracker snapshots are read through certified complete SDK queries without source writes; hidden triage labels, typed edges/non-edge controls and explicit duplicate ground truth are sampled deterministically; TOON and JSON report accuracy, class precision/recall, ten-bin ECE, threshold curves, latency, tokens and per-example provenance; synthetic regressions and unchanged npm/Bun gates pass."
parent: pm-jev-0w3q
comments[13]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-18T03:03:21.067Z",codex-agent,"Plan: read only committed public fleet tracker snapshots through certified complete SDK reads. Deterministic repository-separated sampling; temperature scaling fit on calibration repositories only; validate precision with a one-sided Wilson bound before qualifying any threshold. Serial local-only requests, at most 150 calls, no release."
  "2026-10-18T03:12:07.781Z",codex-agent,"Implemented content-free evaluation receipts, committed public snapshots with no source writes, label-hidden triage, typed-edge labels and deterministic non-edge controls. Temperature fits use separate repository identities and proposal precision excludes none predictions. A serial niced 140-call live comparison is running across six verified public repositories. Existing focused legacy regressions are running alongside new real-temp-tracker tests."
  "2026-10-18T03:32:08.122Z",codex-agent,"Independent behavioural revert proofs: (1) restoring only decideTriage from origin/main makes node --test --test-name-pattern=\"calibrated triage uses\" test/calibrated-decisions.test.ts fail 0/1 at the calibrated-probability assertion. (2) removing only the calibration-repository filter in calibrateObservations makes node --test --test-name-pattern=\"temperature minimizes\" test/decision-calibration.test.ts fail 0/1: held-out label changes move temperature from 0.05 to 20. (3) replacing only the locked opaque settings read in runEvaluationCommand with normalized current.jev makes node --test --test-name-pattern=\"calibrate persists\" test/evaluation-command.test.ts fail 0/1 because the existing keep_alive setting disappears. All mutants exited 1 with assertion failures, no timeouts; all three source files restored byte-for-byte. Tests import TypeScript directly, so no rebuild is needed for these proofs. Corrected focused suite previously passed 14/14; final added identity/retrieval cases are rerunning."
  "2026-10-18T03:50:49.590Z",codex-agent,"Corrected focused suite passes 16/16. All three new modules measured 100 percent statements, branches, functions and lines in the dedicated coverage run. Final policy regressions cover unqualified streaming, changed schemas, missing channels, removal of calibration, model replacement during inference and stricter explicit confidence flags. Calibration defaults to 100 requests (evaluation 40), because a 40-case split cannot reach the 0.9 one-sided precision bound even if perfect. No live target or standard was lowered. SDK operation IDs are invocation-scoped so reapplying an intentionally removed calibration is not mistaken for replay. Compatibility inspection confirms the declared host floor exports both repeatable flags and audited settings mutation; dependency pins and release policy remain unchanged. The first full npm gate passed 184 tests but failed coverage during edits; the first Bun gate exposed a synthetic operation-ID replay bug and missing streaming branches. Those are corrected; neither failed gate is counted as a pass. Final isolated full gates follow."
  "2026-10-18T04:08:49.561Z",codex-agent,"Final isolated release gates pass through the pinned pm runner: npm run release:check and bun run release:check each run 185/185 tests, zero failures/skips/cancellations/todos. Native Node and c8 both report 100 percent lines, branches, functions and statements across all 15 authored sources. Duplication is zero, production audit reports zero findings, changelog checks pass and publication attestation remains valid. The earlier native function gap was a threshold-sort comparator never exercised by uniform synthetic probabilities; mixed-confidence cases now verify selection of the highest-coverage qualifying threshold. Strict tracker health passes with required merge drivers and valid workspace history. Test-result tracking is disabled by existing project policy; these comments retain the sanitized receipts without changing that policy. The release-enable variable is absent and workflow defaults remain disabled. Follow-up pm-jev-w1zj records partial receipts and explicit call counts after endpoint interruption; no incomplete calibration is saved."
  "2026-10-18T04:16:58.510Z",codex-agent,"Bounded live receipt complete: 140 successful serial niced systemOne requests plus one verified failed small-model load attempt, total 141/150. Six public committed tracker snapshots, no source writes. Held-out 4b triage type: n=30, accuracy 40.0%, ECE 0.191 to 0.215; priority: 53.3%, ECE 0.133 to 0.118. Held-out 4b link: n=21, accuracy 47.6%, ECE 0.096 to 0.151. Held-out 0.8b triage type: n=21, accuracy 4.8%, ECE 0.519 to 0.093; priority: 33.3%, ECE 0.380 to 0.112. Every channel threshold remains null at target precision 0.9; calibration authorizes zero proposals. Raw 0.8 confidence gates before other mutation guards accept 3, 0, 0, 0 and 5 held-out decisions respectively. Link/small-model folds are too small for the uncertainty bound even if perfect. On identical 40-item inputs, 4b versus 0.8b raw type accuracy is 50.0% versus 12.5%, priority 60.0% versus 30.0%. Full class metrics, ten-bin reliability, curves, source/model/data digests, request latency and tokens are in calibration/public-report-v1.json. Audited SDK settings contain all three model/task receipts; no target was lowered. Packed Node and native Bun CLI smoke checks pass four scenarios: repeated source flags, JSON eval, variadic calibration with actual SDK persistence, and default TOON. Synthetic models and public-visibility doubles were used for install checks. The pinned linked focused command passes 16/16 tests. Release remains disabled; source and gate code are stable."
  "2026-10-18T04:28:42.920Z",codex-agent,"PR https://github.com/unbraind/pm-jev/pull/24 is open, not merged. First source head cb157020071174caabdc6a78ecd252e0cc388728 passed GitHub CI test (22), test (26) and CodeQL. CI run: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-jev/actions/runs/39096845795 . Local npm and Bun release gates each passed 185/185 tests and unchanged 100 percent statements/branches/functions/lines across 15 authored sources. All 140 successful live-request receipts replay exactly and match SDK project settings; the single failed load attempt makes the total 141/150. Final packed-artifact Node/native-Bun smoke checks pass 4/4, and strict tracker health passes with required merge drivers. All six source repositories are still public, with unchanged commit/data digests; all have zero explicit duplicate targets, so dedupe has synthetic ground-truth coverage only. All five measured channels remain unqualified at target precision 0.9. Source code and data are final; this tracker-only closeout commit records CI evidence and releases implementation claims. Its exact remote head checks will be verified before delivery. Automatic reviewer neutral/skipped statuses are not approvals. Release remains disabled, and items remain in_progress for orchestrator verification."
  "2026-10-18T05:28:02.892Z",codex-agent,"Round 1 PR #24: read all three unresolved CodeRabbit threads and latest review. Verified sibling duplicates can enter positive single-label dedupe rows. Plan: exclude siblings while retaining canonical target; add a real committed synthetic tracker regression and independent behavioral revert proof. Re-run only synthetic dedupe evaluation; published live table remains unaffected because dedupe live validation was synthetic-only."
  "2026-10-18T05:30:10.882Z",codex-agent,"Synthetic-only dedupe revalidation: real committed tracker built from test/fixtures/evaluation.json plus an explicitly labelled sibling; 4/4 model requests (2 canonical-target positives, 2 none controls), accuracy 1.0, NLL 0, zero retrieval misses, and source tracker byte identity preserved. Both siblings are absent from every candidate list and the canonical target remains in each positive. The published live table is unaffected: dedupe live validation was synthetic-only; no live model receipt rerun."
  "2026-10-18T05:30:51.183Z",codex-agent,"Independent behavioral revert proof: restore only the old positive candidate filter inside buildExamples, keeping all other fixes and tests; npm run build succeeds, then node --test --test-name-pattern=\"synthetic dedupe evaluation excludes\" test/evaluation-command.test.ts exits 1 because sibling ids appear in candidate lists. Fixed source restored byte-for-byte and rebuilt. Corrected synthetic-only evaluation passes 4 examples with zero retrieval misses; published live table is unaffected (dedupe live validation was synthetic-only)."
  "2026-10-18T05:31:38.656Z",codex-agent,"Fixed-state linked verification: pm test pm-jev-82ip --run --only-last --progress passes 7/7 tests (node --test test/tracker-evaluation.test.ts test/evaluation-command.test.ts), zero failures/skips/cancellations/todo. Combined focused result 19/19; synthetic dedupe requests 4/4 with canonical positives and sibling-free controls."
  "2026-10-18T05:42:19.654Z",codex-agent,"Round 1 final verification: npm run release:check and bun run release:check under separate fresh HOME directories with GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL=/dev/null and GIT_CONFIG_NOSYSTEM=1 each pass 188/188 tests, zero failures/skips/cancellations/todo; unchanged 100 percent coverage across all 15 authored sources, zero duplication and zero production audit findings. Focused linked tests pass 19/19; all four independent behavioral reverts fail. Synthetic dedupe revalidation passes four requests with two canonical positives, two none controls, zero retrieval misses and byte-identical source tracker. Published live table and persisted live receipt remain unchanged; dedupe live validation was synthetic-only. No new PM CLI/SDK defect identified. Items remain in progress for orchestrator verification; next steps are push, three thread replies and bounded CI wait."
  "2026-10-18T05:45:56.900Z",codex-agent,"Post-push integration blocker: main advanced during local gates to 81bce989f79bb4d9e66e027184cd16574803ed19 (PR #23 PM closeout). PR #24 now reports mergeable=false/dirty, so pull-request CI and CodeQL do not start. Its PM-only changes diverge in history/pm-jev-2mg8.jsonl and history/pm-jev-3ntg.jsonl: appending untouched incoming records to the branch fails verifyHistoryChain with before_hash_mismatch at entries 39 and 29 respectively. The installed merge preview proposes union_reanchor; no tracked history was changed and its two scratch receipts were removed. Under the explicit no-reanchor/no-history-rewrite rule, that result cannot be applied. No PR was merged. Existing CI workflow was dispatched directly on source head 8b2002e0f3b5736a0977dec17f55cfdc0659b685; final evidence head will receive its own exact-head dispatch. Main integration and pull-request CodeQL remain separate open risks for the orchestrator."
